$DIR/main.p:6:7: string literal not terminated
    A string, rune or number is not written correctly, or the file contains a
    character that is not allowed outside strings and comments. Strings in
    double quotes must end on the same line; use a raw string in backquotes for
    text over several lines. Rune literals in single quotes hold exactly one
    character. Curly quotation marks, often pasted from a word processor, are
    not quotes to the compiler.
    (see "Lexical elements" in the Plutonium spec, section 4)
    (run "pluto explain E1008" for a longer explanation)
